-- wra2-s49-jsa-requirements.l4: Welfare Reform Act 2012 (UK) s 49, claimant responsibilities for jobseeker's allowance after the introduction of universal credit.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Part wra2. Host Act short name: JSA = Jobseekers Act 1995.
-- Source: inputs/ukpga-2012-5.txt (a converter script's plain-text rendering; not the official text).
-- Section 49 repeals JSA 1(2)(a) and (c) and substitutes JSA 6 to 10: work-related requirements (6 to 6I), higher-level sanctions (6J),
-- other sanctions (6K), delegation (6L). It reuses the helpers of the s 46 module (three-valued logic, good reason) and the s 44 award test.
-- Mapping to the core (seam 9 of PLAN.md): JSA 6J -> `jobseeker's allowance higher-level sanction after universal credit`;
-- JSA 6K -> `jobseeker's allowance other sanction after universal credit`.
-- JSA 6(2), 6B(1), 6C(1), 6D(1), 6E(1) map to the core's `Work-related requirement`: the four requirements of this Act's JSA.

§ `s 49 JSA 6: work-related requirements`

-- src:695 | (1) The following provisions of this Act provide for the Secretary of State to impose work-related requirements with which claimants must comply for the purposes of this Act.
@ref s 49 JSA 6(1) (src:695)
GIVEN `a work-related requirement has been imposed on the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49 JSA 6(1) the claimant must comply with the work-related requirement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a work-related requirement has been imposed on the claimant`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the provisions "provide for the Secretary of State to impose work-related requirements with which claimants must comply"; none has been imposed
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 49 JSA 6 what a requirement asks of the claimant` IS ONE OF
    `s 49 JSA 6B(1) to participate in one or more work-focused interviews as specified by the Secretary of State`
    `s 49 JSA 6C(1) to take particular action specified by the Secretary of State to make paid work more likely in the opinion of the Secretary of State`
    `s 49 JSA 6D(1) to take all reasonable action and any particular action specified by the Secretary of State for the purpose of obtaining paid work`
    `s 49 JSA 6E(1) to be available for work`
    `s 49 JSA 6 to do something else`

-- src:711 | (1) In this Act a “work-focused interview requirement” is a requirement that a claimant participate in one or more work-focused interviews as specified by the Secretary of State.
@ref s 49 JSA 6B(1) (src:711)
GIVEN `what the requirement asks` IS A `s 49 JSA 6 what a requirement asks of the claimant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 49 JSA 6B(1) the requirement is a work-focused interview requirement` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a “work-focused interview requirement” is a requirement that a claimant participate in one or more work-focused interviews as specified by the Secretary of State" (a definition; "is", not "means", see NOTES)
    `what the requirement asks` EQUALS `s 49 JSA 6B(1) to participate in one or more work-focused interviews as specified by the Secretary of State`

-- src:716 | (1) In this Act a “work preparation requirement” is a requirement that a claimant take particular action specified by the Secretary of State for the purpose of making it more likely in the opinion of the Secretary of State that the claimant will obtain paid work (or more paid work or better-paid work).
@ref s 49 JSA 6C(1) (src:716)
GIVEN `what the requirement asks` IS A `s 49 JSA 6 what a requirement asks of the claimant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 49 JSA 6C(1) the requirement is a work preparation requirement` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a “work preparation requirement” is a requirement that a claimant take particular action specified by the Secretary of State for the purpose of making it more likely in the opinion of the Secretary of State that the claimant will obtain paid work"
    `what the requirement asks` EQUALS `s 49 JSA 6C(1) to take particular action specified by the Secretary of State to make paid work more likely in the opinion of the Secretary of State`

-- src:727 | (1) In this Part a “work search requirement” is a requirement that a claimant take—
-- src:728 | (a) all reasonable action, and
-- src:729 | (b) any particular action specified by the Secretary of State,
-- src:730 | for the purpose of obtaining paid work (or more paid work or better-paid work).
@ref s 49 JSA 6D(1) (src:727-730)
GIVEN `what the requirement asks` IS A `s 49 JSA 6 what a requirement asks of the claimant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 49 JSA 6D(1) the requirement is a work search requirement` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a “work search requirement” is a requirement that a claimant take (a) all reasonable action, and (b) any particular action specified by the Secretary of State, for the purpose of obtaining paid work"
    `what the requirement asks` EQUALS `s 49 JSA 6D(1) to take all reasonable action and any particular action specified by the Secretary of State for the purpose of obtaining paid work`

-- src:747 | (1) In this Act a “work availability requirement” is a requirement that a claimant be available for work.
@ref s 49 JSA 6E(1) (src:747)
GIVEN `what the requirement asks` IS A `s 49 JSA 6 what a requirement asks of the claimant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 49 JSA 6E(1) the requirement is a work availability requirement` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a “work availability requirement” is a requirement that a claimant be available for work"
    `what the requirement asks` EQUALS `s 49 JSA 6E(1) to be available for work`

-- src:696 | (2) In this Act “work-related requirement” means—
-- src:697 | (a) a work-focused interview requirement (see section 6B);
-- src:698 | (b) a work preparation requirement (see section 6C);
-- src:699 | (c) a work search requirement (see section 6D);
-- src:700 | (d) a work availability requirement (see section 6E).
@ref s 49 JSA 6(2) (src:696-700)
GIVEN `what the requirement asks` IS A `s 49 JSA 6 what a requirement asks of the claimant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 49 JSA 6(2) the requirement is a work-related requirement` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“work-related requirement” means (a) a work-focused interview requirement ... (d) a work availability requirement"
        `s 49 JSA 6B(1) the requirement is a work-focused interview requirement` `what the requirement asks`
    OR  `s 49 JSA 6C(1) the requirement is a work preparation requirement` `what the requirement asks`
    OR  `s 49 JSA 6D(1) the requirement is a work search requirement` `what the requirement asks`
    OR  `s 49 JSA 6E(1) the requirement is a work availability requirement` `what the requirement asks`

-- src:696 | (2) In this Act “work-related requirement” means—
-- src:697 | (a) a work-focused interview requirement (see section 6B);
-- src:698 | (b) a work preparation requirement (see section 6C);
-- src:699 | (c) a work search requirement (see section 6D);
-- src:700 | (d) a work availability requirement (see section 6E).
@ref s 49 JSA 6(2) (src:696-700)
GIVEN `the requirement` IS A `Work-related requirement`
GIVETH A STRING
`s 49 JSA 6(2) the section that gives the meaning of the requirement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the requirement`
    WHEN `work-focused interview requirement` THEN "6B"
    WHEN `work preparation requirement` THEN "6C"
    WHEN `work search requirement` THEN "6D"
    WHEN `work availability requirement` THEN "6E"

§ `s 49 JSA 6A: claimant commitment`

-- src:702 | (1) A claimant commitment is a record of a claimant's responsibilities in relation to an award of a jobseeker's allowance.
@ref s 49 JSA 6A(1) (src:702)
GIVEN `the document is a record of a claimant's responsibilities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the award the record is in relation to` IS A Benefit
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 49 JSA 6A(1) the document is a claimant commitment` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A claimant commitment is a record of a claimant's responsibilities in relation to an award of a jobseeker's allowance" (a definition; "is", not "means", see NOTES)
        `the document is a record of a claimant's responsibilities`
    AND `s 44 JSA 9(1) the award is an award of a jobseeker's allowance` `the award the record is in relation to`

-- src:703 | (2) A claimant commitment is to be prepared by the Secretary of State and may be reviewed and updated as the Secretary of State thinks fit.
-- src:847 | (1) The functions of the Secretary of State under sections 6 to 6I may be exercised by, or by the employees of, such person as the Secretary of State may authorise for the purpose (an “authorised person”).
@ref s 49 JSA 6A(2) with 6L(1) (src:703 src:847)
GIVEN `who prepared the claimant commitment` IS AN Authority
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49 JSA 6A(2) the claimant commitment was prepared by the Secretary of State` MEANS
    CONSIDER `who prepared the claimant commitment`
    WHEN `the Secretary of State` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- JSA 6L(1): the functions of the Secretary of State under sections 6 to 6I may be exercised by an authorised person
    WHEN `an authorised person` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "is to be prepared by the Secretary of State" says nothing of preparation by anyone else
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:704 | (3) A claimant commitment is to be in such form as the Secretary of State thinks fit.
@ref s 49 JSA 6A(3) (src:704)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State thinks the form fit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 49 JSA 6A(3) the claimant commitment is in the form the Secretary of State thinks fit` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A claimant commitment is to be in such form as the Secretary of State thinks fit"
    `the Secretary of State thinks the form fit`

-- src:705 | (4) A claimant commitment is to include—
-- src:706 | (a) a record of the requirements that the claimant must comply with under this Act (or such of them as the Secretary of State considers it appropriate to include),
-- src:707 | (b) any prescribed information, and
-- src:708 | (c) any other information the Secretary of State considers it appropriate to include.
@ref s 49 JSA 6A(4) (src:705-708)
GIVEN `it includes a record of the requirements the claimant must comply with, or of such of them as the Secretary of State considers appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it includes the prescribed information` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it includes any other information the Secretary of State considers appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49 JSA 6A(4) the claimant commitment includes what the subsection requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A claimant commitment is to include (a) a record of the requirements that the claimant must comply with"
        IF NOT `it includes a record of the requirements the claimant must comply with, or of such of them as the Secretary of State considers appropriate`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A claimant commitment is to include ... (c) any other information the Secretary of State considers it appropriate to include"
        IF NOT `it includes any other information the Secretary of State considers appropriate`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE CONSIDER `it includes the prescribed information`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) any prescribed information"
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): what information is prescribed is left to regulations
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- src:709 | (5) For the purposes of this Act a claimant accepts a claimant commitment if, and only if, the claimant accepts the most up-to-date version of it in such manner as may be prescribed.
@ref s 49 JSA 6A(5) (src:709)
GIVEN `the claimant accepted the most up-to-date version of the claimant commitment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant accepted it in the manner prescribed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49 JSA 6A(5) the claimant accepts the claimant commitment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "accepts a claimant commitment if, and only if, the claimant accepts the most up-to-date version of it"
        IF NOT `the claimant accepted the most up-to-date version of the claimant commitment`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE CONSIDER `the claimant accepted it in the manner prescribed`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if, and only if, ... accepts ... in such manner as may be prescribed" -- accepted, but not in the prescribed manner
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the manner of acceptance is prescribed in regulations that are not among the sources
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§ `s 49 JSA 6B to 6E: the four requirements`

-- src:712 | (2) A work-focused interview is an interview for prescribed purposes relating to work or work preparation.
@ref s 49 JSA 6B(2) (src:712)
GIVEN `the interview is for prescribed purposes` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the purposes relate to work or work preparation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49 JSA 6B(2) the interview is a work-focused interview` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A work-focused interview is an interview for prescribed purposes relating to work or work preparation"
        IF NOT `the purposes relate to work or work preparation`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): which purposes are prescribed is left to regulations
        OTHERWISE `the interview is for prescribed purposes`

DECLARE `s 49 JSA 6B(3) purpose` IS ONE OF
    `s 49 JSA 6B(3) making it more likely, in the opinion of the Secretary of State, that the claimant will obtain paid work (or more paid work or better-paid work)`
    `s 49 JSA 6B(3) some other purpose`

-- src:713 | (3) The purposes which may be prescribed under subsection (2) include in particular that of making it more likely in the opinion of the Secretary of State that the claimant will obtain paid work (or more paid work or better-paid work).
@ref s 49 JSA 6B(3) (src:713)
GIVEN `the purpose` IS A `s 49 JSA 6B(3) purpose`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49 JSA 6B(3) the purpose may be prescribed under subsection (2)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the purpose`
    WHEN `s 49 JSA 6B(3) making it more likely, in the opinion of the Secretary of State, that the claimant will obtain paid work (or more paid work or better-paid work)` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "The purposes which may be prescribed ... include in particular" one purpose and do not close the list
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 49 JSA 6B(4) matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 49 JSA 6B(4) how the interview is to take place`
    `s 49 JSA 6B(4) when the interview is to take place`
    `s 49 JSA 6B(4) where the interview is to take place`
    `s 49 JSA 6B(4) some other matter`

-- src:714 | (4) The Secretary of State may specify how, when and where a work-focused interview is to take place.
@ref s 49 JSA 6B(4) (src:714)
GIVEN `the matter` IS A `s 49 JSA 6B(4) matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49 JSA 6B(4) the Secretary of State may specify that matter` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the matter`
    WHEN `s 49 JSA 6B(4) how the interview is to take place` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 49 JSA 6B(4) when the interview is to take place` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 49 JSA 6B(4) where the interview is to take place` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "how, when and where" are the matters the Secretary of State may specify; the grant says nothing of others
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 49 JSA 6C(3) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 49 JSA 6C(3)(a) attending a skills assessment`
    `s 49 JSA 6C(3)(b) improving personal presentation`
    `s 49 JSA 6C(3)(c) participating in training`
    `s 49 JSA 6C(3)(d) participating in an employment programme`
    `s 49 JSA 6C(3)(e) undertaking work experience or a work placement`
    `s 49 JSA 6C(3)(f) developing a business plan`
    `s 49 JSA 6C(3)(g) an action prescribed for the purpose in subsection (1)`
    `s 49 JSA 6C(3) some other action`

-- src:718 | (3) Action which may be specified under subsection (1) includes in particular—
-- src:719 | (a) attending a skills assessment;
-- src:720 | (b) improving personal presentation;
-- src:721 | (c) participating in training;
-- src:722 | (d) participating in an employment programme;
-- src:723 | (e) undertaking work experience or a work placement;
-- src:724 | (f) developing a business plan;
-- src:725 | (g) any action prescribed for the purpose in subsection (1).
@ref s 49 JSA 6C(3) (src:718-725)
GIVEN `the action` IS A `s 49 JSA 6C(3) action`
      `the action is prescribed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49 JSA 6C(3) the action may be specified under subsection (1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the action`
    WHEN `s 49 JSA 6C(3)(a) attending a skills assessment` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 49 JSA 6C(3)(b) improving personal presentation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 49 JSA 6C(3)(c) participating in training` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 49 JSA 6C(3)(d) participating in an employment programme` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 49 JSA 6C(3)(e) undertaking work experience or a work placement` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 49 JSA 6C(3)(f) developing a business plan` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): (g) "any action prescribed for the purpose" is prescribed in regulations that are not among the sources
    WHEN `s 49 JSA 6C(3)(g) an action prescribed for the purpose in subsection (1)` THEN `the action is prescribed`
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "Action which may be specified ... includes in particular" and does not close the list
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:717 | (2) The Secretary of State may under subsection (1) specify the time to be devoted to any particular action.
@ref s 49 JSA 6C(2) (src:717)
GIVEN `the matter is the time to be devoted to a particular action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
