        IF `the matter is the time to be devoted to a particular action`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is of "the time to be devoted to any particular action" and says nothing of other matters
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:731 | (2) The Secretary of State may under subsection (1)(b) specify the time to be devoted to any particular action.
@ref s 49 JSA 6D(2) (src:731)
GIVEN `the matter is the time to be devoted to a particular action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49 JSA 6D(2) the Secretary of State may specify the time to be devoted to the action` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the matter is the time to be devoted to a particular action`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is of "the time to be devoted to any particular action" and says nothing of other matters
