§ `s 49 JSA 6J: higher-level sanctions`

-- src:801 | (d) by reason of misconduct, or voluntarily and for no good reason, ceases paid work or loses pay.
-- src:804 | (b) by reason of misconduct, or voluntarily and for no good reason, ceased paid work or lost pay.
-- src:805 | (4) For the purposes of subsections (2) and (3) regulations may provide—
-- src:806 | (a) for circumstances in which ceasing to work or losing pay is to be treated as occurring or not occurring by reason of misconduct or voluntarily;
-- src:807 | (b) for loss of pay below a prescribed level to be disregarded.
@ref s 49 JSA 6J(2)(d) with 6J(3)(b) and 6J(4) (src:801 src:804 src:805-807)
GIVEN `the claimant ceased paid work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant lost pay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was by reason of misconduct, as regulations under subsection (4)(a) treat it` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it was voluntary, as regulations under subsection (4)(a) treat it` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the claimant had a good reason` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the loss of pay was below the prescribed level and so disregarded` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49 JSA 6J(2)(d) the claimant ceased paid work or lost pay in a way that counts` MEANS
    `s 46 JSA 19 Kleene both` `ceased work or lost pay that counts` `by misconduct or voluntarily and for no good reason`
    WHERE
        `ceased work or lost pay that counts` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the claimant ceased paid work` THEN JUST TRUE
                IF `the claimant lost pay` THEN `s 46 JSA 19 Kleene not` `the loss of pay was below the prescribed level and so disregarded`
                OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
        `by misconduct or voluntarily and for no good reason` MEANS
            `s 46 JSA 19 Kleene either` `it was by reason of misconduct, as regulations under subsection (4)(a) treat it`
                (`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene both` `it was voluntary, as regulations under subsection (4)(a) treat it` (`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene not` `the claimant had a good reason`))

